{"name":"Cut the Mustard","hex":"#ba7f38","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cut the mustard","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To achieve the expected standard; to be effective or good enough; to suffice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cut_the_mustard"}],"entries":[{"title":"English-language idioms","blocks":[{"text":"An idiom is a common word or phrase with a figurative, non-literal meaning that is understood culturally and differs from what its composite words' denotations would suggest; i.e. the words together have a meaning that is different from the dictionary definitions of the individual words. By another definition, an idiom is a speech form or an expression of a given language that is peculiar to itself grammatically or cannot be understood from the individual meanings of its elements. For example, an English speaker would understand the phrase \"kick the bucket\" to mean \"to die\" – and also to actually kick a bucket. Furthermore, they would understand when each meaning is being used in context."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Bookman_Ornament_9617_%28bookshelf%29.svg/330px-Bookman_Ornament_9617_%28bookshelf%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English-language_idioms"},{"title":"Mustard (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Mustard is a dull/dark yellow color that resembles culinary mustard. It is similar to the color Flax."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mustard_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Plaster_wall_in_%22baby_mustard%22_color_-_20070925.jpg/250px-Plaster_wall_in_%22baby_mustard%22_color_-_20070925.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a9/Plaster_wall_in_%22baby_mustard%22_color_-_20070925.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Plaster_wall_in_%22baby_mustard%22_color_-_20070925.jpg/250px-Plaster_wall_in_%22baby_mustard%22_color_-_20070925.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A plaster wall painted a dark shade of mustard called \"baby mustard\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlaster_wall_in_%22baby_mustard%22_color_-_20070925.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Mustard_French_condiment.jpg/500px-Mustard_French_condiment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Mustard_French_condiment.jpg/500px-Mustard_French_condiment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A jar of mustard","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMustard_French_condiment.jpg"}],"sounds":{"cut the mustard":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/47/En-au-cut_the_mustard.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/47/En-au-cut_the_mustard.ogg/En-au-cut_the_mustard.ogg.mp3"}]}}}